Research Engine Phase 8: the project brief, the language corpus, waves across runs

The project brief: research.brief (client, business question, the decision
the findings inform, background, stakeholders, deadline, deliverables) on the
design; set_research { brief } merges field by field; nine sentence forms
("the client is Acme Foods", "this study informs the decision to …", "add
stakeholder: …", "what is the brief?"); the editor's Brief section with
"copy from another project" (GET /api/briefs); carried into the outline the
model reads, the proposal (opens with it), the report and the deck (the
client, the question and the decision), and the workflow (the business
question offered as the objective).

The language regression corpus: History records the engine's reading on
every turn (engine, engineCategory, engineReason, ops, selected);
packages/engine/src/languageCorpus.ts builds a corpus from the history and
replays it against the engine as it is (same / better / worse / changed, the
backlog of the model's sentences most said first); the History tab shows the
project's language and exports the corpus (POST /api/copilot/corpus);
packages/engine/corpus/brand-tracker.json (105 sentences) is replayed by the
engine's tests; scripts/corpus-replay.mjs replays or records a file.

Waves across runs: every run measures the design's KPIs on its own data
(top-N-box share, mean, NPS, share of an option) and, when a previous
comparable run exists (same environment, same dataset kind), carries the
comparison — KPI deltas with their significance (two-proportion test, Welch's
t from the summaries) and direction, the planned findings matched by what
they test (new / stronger / weaker / reversed / same, and those gone), the
verdicts that changed — in the Findings tab, the brief the model reads (the
gate knows the deltas), a deck slide after the summary and a report section
after the hypotheses. Migration 0049 (kpis, since) with insert fallbacks.

